{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgiCjFXpBJHruJNn9GSNw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. The patch is in place and verified.\n\n**→ What changed.** `router.py` now has a third rule, `_is_eligibility_query`, that sends questions about **age, minors, countries, residency, and service availability** to account_security. It runs after the exchange-rate and PIN rules, so the earlier corrections keep priority.\n\n**→ Guards.** The rule stays silent when the message has **dispute signals, money-movement words** (send, transfer, top up, withdraw, balance, payment) or **cost words** (fee, rate, exchange, currency, ATM, cash). Brand names such as \"American Express\" are stripped before matching, since the evidence has one such trap.\n\n**→ Test results.** Command: `.venv/bin/python -I test_router.py <task dir>`.\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Evidence rows | 32/32 correct |\n| Extra sanity cases (old corrections, transfers, disputes, fees) | 20/20 correct |\n| Rule disabled (negative test) | 16 rows fail, so the test is a real guard |\n\n**→ NOTES.md** is written, 188 words, under the limit.\n\n**→ Risk.** A named region plus \"use\" routes to account_security, as the evidence row \"What countries can I use the card in?\" demands. A hidden message like \"Can I use my card in Spain?\" will go the same way. That follows the evidence, but it is the one judgment call in the patch."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":775,"cache_read_input_tokens":78845,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":775},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"31534dd2-3263-4e31-a65a-ea895d2429ba","uuid":"83c119b2-4e15-4ee4-87